  "abstract": "If disposing of this product, please recycle the paper.This monograph explores the integration of the United Nations (UN) Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) into World Trade Organisation (WTO) law, aiming to safeguard environmental and social interests from the negative externalities of international trade.It is based on research conducted during my doctoral studies at the University of Lausanne from 2018 to 2022.My initial motivation for this research stemmed from my concern about environmental pollution in my hometown of Beijing.My supervisor, Professor Andreas R. Ziegler, is interested in interdisciplinary research on trade and environmental and social issues.He encouraged and supported me throughout this journey, introducing me to the theory of global constitutionalism, which provided valuable insights into the nexus of trade",
